WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.717
The Federal Compliance series
arranged its material by layer;

2
00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:07.313
the workbook books arrange it by
the question a reader brings.

3
00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:12.561
Chapter 12 maps each part of the series
to the book that carries it now,

4
00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.324
and Appendix A indexes 149 controls.

5
00:00:15.324 --> 00:00:20.725
Where a book and the older series disagree,
the book is the later, footnoted text.

6
00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:23.163
Two dependency claims explain the map.

7
00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:28.001
The naming and identity floor comes first:
you can't inventory what you can't name.

8
00:00:28.001 --> 00:00:30.686
Assurance comes last,
because the package can

9
00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:33.725
only report what the earlier
books made observable.

10
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:39.108
Build everything on the map and risk still
remains, in six kinds: self-assessment,

11
00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:43.757
until an independent assessor confirms
it; what automation can't see;

12
00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:47.916
risk inherited from providers;
evidence that stops arriving;

13
00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:51.831
risks outside control evaluation,
such as insider threat;

14
00:00:51.831 --> 00:00:55.338
and design not yet built, or
features not yet shipped.

15
00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:56.674
Write the remainder down.

16
00:00:56.674 --> 00:00:59.494
A package that lists
what's proven, asserted,

17
00:00:59.494 --> 00:01:04.420
inherited and accepted gives the
authorizing official a risk they can see.
